From: pi-286-games maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] dynrec: select the ARM generator for ARM-mode ARMv6 builds

The ARM hard-float cross compiler defines __THUMB_INTERWORK__ even when
compiling with -marm. The ARMV4LE switcher consequently selected the obsolete
Thumb-interwork generator, which contains an invalid duplicate template
parameter list on modern GCC. ARM1176 builds deliberately emit ARM code, so
only choose that generator when the compiler is actually compiling Thumb.

---
 src/cpu/core_dynrec/risc_armv4le.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cpu/core_dynrec/risc_armv4le.h b/src/cpu/core_dynrec/risc_armv4le.h
index 4975476..8134a8f 100644
--- a/src/cpu/core_dynrec/risc_armv4le.h
+++ b/src/cpu/core_dynrec/risc_armv4le.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #if C_TARGETCPU == ARMV7LE
 	#include "risc_armv4le-o3.h"
 #else
-	#if defined(__THUMB_INTERWORK__)
+	#if defined(__thumb__) && defined(__THUMB_INTERWORK__)
 		#include "risc_armv4le-thumb-iw.h"
 	#else
 		#include "risc_armv4le-o3.h"
